WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.533
Tools that see and keep.

2
00:00:01.693 --> 00:00:03.875
Some art tools do not use paint at all.

3
00:00:04.035 --> 00:00:05.568
A camera keeps a picture.

4
00:00:05.728 --> 00:00:08.235
A magnifying glass shows tiny details.

5
00:00:08.395 --> 00:00:11.182
A drawing app lets you draw and change it again.

6
00:00:11.342 --> 00:00:13.989
Always ask a person before you take their photo.

7
00:00:14.689 --> 00:00:15.850
Close or far.

8
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.700
A close-up photo shows one small thing, very big, like the spots on a ladybird.

9
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.622
A far-away photo shows a lot, all small, like a whole mountain.

10
00:00:24.782 --> 00:00:27.290
Move closer or step back until it looks right.

11
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.244
Move, then draw.

12
00:00:29.404 --> 00:00:32.004
When you move, your body makes lines in the air.

13
00:00:32.164 --> 00:00:34.301
Hopping forward makes a zigzag.

14
00:00:34.461 --> 00:00:35.807
A spin is a circle.

15
00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:37.639
A sway is a wavy line.

16
00:00:37.799 --> 00:00:40.075
Move first, then draw the line you made.

17
00:00:40.775 --> 00:00:41.936
Make it move.

18
00:00:42.096 --> 00:00:46.368
A cartoon is lots of pictures, each a little different, shown very fast.

19
00:00:46.528 --> 00:00:47.968
That is animation.

20
00:00:48.128 --> 00:00:52.865
A flip book is the simplest kind: draw on every page, then flip.
